      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: DRAINAGE SYSTEM"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Drainage patterns are classified into Dendritic, Trellis, Radial, Rectangular, and Centripetal patterns based on topography and rock structure.",
        "A river's journey is divided into three distinct stages: Upper Course (youthful/erosional), Middle Course (mature/transportation), and Lower Course (old age/depositional).",
        "River landforms are broadly categorized into Erosional Landforms (e.g., gorges, waterfalls) and Depositional Landforms (e.g., deltas, alluvial fans).",
        "Understanding watersheds and drainage basins is essential for analyzing river flow and catchment characteristics."
      ],
      "id": "hkhpmzg"
    },
