    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Differentiate drainage patterns: Dendritic (tree-like), Radial (flowing outwards from a central high peak), Centripetal (flowing inward into a central depression), and Trellis (tributaries joining at right angles).",
        "Classify landforms correctly: Gorges, Canyons, Waterfalls, and Potholes are Erosional; Floodplains, Oxbow Lakes, Natural Levees, and Deltas are Depositional.",
        "Focus on SSC SSC-frequently asked features of Upper Course (steep gradient, maximum vertical erosion) vs. Lower Course (gentle slope, maximum deposition)."
      ],
